re\'s the Python code that satisfies the requirements and provides the final result:\n\n```python\nfrom object_detection_tool import Execution\n\ndef detect_persimons(image_path, labels, threshold, model_size, padding):\n  detected_objects = Execution(image_path, labels, threshold, model_size, padding).execute()\n  \n  # Define a regular expression to match people wearing red shirts\n  people_pattern = r\'member\\s+\\(.*?\\)\'\n  \n  # Count the number of people wearing red shirts\n  red_shirt_people_count = sum(1 for subject in detected_objects[\'output\'] if people_pattern.search(subject[\'label\']))\n  \n  return red_shirt_people_count\n\nresult = detect_persimons("/home/stud/wxie/BLINK_Dataset/Counting/val/images/val_Counting_8_image_1.jpg", [\'person\'], 0.5, \'tiny\', 20)\nprint(f"The number of people wearing red shirts is: {result}")\n```\n\nNote: The above code assumes that you have installed the "object_detection_tool" package. If you don\'t, you can install it using pip:\n\n```python\n!pip install object_detection_tool\n```'
